B.apR=new A.K('Is the big number the temperature or "feels like"?','The big number is the air temperature; the small one in parentheses is "feels like". Clothes are chosen by "feels like" \u2014 humidity makes it feel warmer, wind makes it feel colder.')
B.api=new A.K('"Now" and the graph show slightly different numbers.','"Now" is the current observation; the graph is the hourly forecast, so they can differ by a degree or two. The time next to the date is when the forecast was last fetched.')
B.apD=new A.K("What is the shading on the graph?","The pale yellow shading is daylight (sunrise to sunset). The blue band is when you're out \u2014 from the time you leave to the time you get back, set in Settings. The high and low numbers are taken inside that band.")
B.apb=new A.K("What happens when I tap the graph?","Tap or drag left and right to see the temperature at that time. Tap outside the graph to close it.")
B.ap7=new A.K("What are the bars at the bottom of the graph?","Chance of rain. The drop and bars appear only when some hour is 20% or more; at 50% or more they turn darker and the app says to take an umbrella.")
B.ap_=new A.K("When do the umbrella, wind and UV signs appear?","Umbrella: chance of rain 50% or more. Wind: 30 km/h (about 19 mph) or more. UV is always shown as Low, Medium or High; on High days (UV 6+) the picture adds sunglasses while the sun is up. Under a 20% chance of rain, the sky shows cloudy instead of rain.")
B.apS=new A.K("What are the Home / Office buttons?","They appear only if you added a work location more than 20 km from home. Tap one to see that place's weather and graph. The outfit uses work weather for midday only.")
B.agh=s([B.apR,B.api,B.apD,B.apb,B.ap7,B.ap_,B.apS],t.Wy)
B.ap1=new A.K("Reading the screen",B.agh)
B.ap9=new A.K("It's warm out \u2014 why is there a jacket?","The app looks at the whole day in three parts: morning, midday and evening. If the morning or evening is cool, it adds one layer you can take off. Morning and evening mean the hour before and after you leave and get back \u2014 set both in Settings.")
B.ap6=new A.K('What does "off at noon" mean?',"That layer is for the morning and evening, but midday is too warm for it. Wear it out, take it off at noon, put it back on later.")
B.apB=new A.K("It's afternoon, but the picture still shows the morning outfit.",'The picture is what to wear when you leave in the morning \u2014 you get dressed once a day. When it warms up, take off the layer marked "off at noon".')
B.aoQ=new A.K("Why long pants on days with a jacket?","You can take off a jacket at noon, but you can't change pants. Shorts show up only when the morning and evening are warm too.")
B.apy=new A.K("Why three outfits?","All three are equally warm; only color, fabric and fit differ. Pick the one you like. The four colors under the picture are a palette to match with clothes you already own.")
B.aoW=new A.K("Where do I change when I leave and get back?",'In Settings, under "When you head out and get back", drag the two handles on the line. Weekdays and weekends can differ; if you leave weekends unset, they follow weekdays. The outfit and the graph band update right away.')
B.apj=new A.K("How do I change the style or men's/women's clothes?","In Settings, pick a weekday style and a weekend style (Casual, Office, Sporty, Street) and Men's or Women's. Style changes only the kind of clothes, not how warm they are.")
B.aoN=new A.K("What is the Look archive?","Settings \u2192 Look archive shows every outfit the app can suggest, by weather. Filter it by men's/women's and style.")
B.apx=new A.K("Where do I see tomorrow's outfit?","Tap the Tomorrow card at the bottom of Today to open it full size, just like today. The forecast can still change, so check again in the morning.")
B.a5l=s([B.ap9,B.ap6,B.apB,B.aoQ,B.apy,B.aoW,B.apj,B.aoN,B.apx],t.Wy)
B.apJ=new A.K("Outfits",B.a5l)
B.aoP=new A.K('What happens when I tap "Too warm / Just right / Too cold"?','Your personal adjustment moves a little. "Too warm" means lighter clothes next time, "too cold" means warmer ones. It learns fast for the first 10 answers, then slowly. It asks once a day, in the evening.')
B.aoX=new A.K("I want the app to start learning from scratch.",'Tap "Reset learning" at the bottom of Settings. Your answers are erased and it starts again from the body type you picked at the start (Runs cold / Normal / Runs warm).')
B.Xb=s([B.aoP,B.aoX],t.Wy)
B.aoZ=new A.K("Fitting your body",B.Xb)
B.aoY=new A.K("Can I see outfits for my kids?","Add a kid under Settings \u2192 Kids and name buttons appear at the top of Today. One tap changes whose outfit you see. With no kids, the buttons stay hidden.")
B.apL=new A.K("How are kids' outfits different?","Kids get casual kids' clothes based on the home forecast. Each kid's \"Too warm / Too cold\" answers are learned separately. Kids' names never leave the phone.")
B.a2m=s([B.aoY,B.apL],t.Wy)
B.aoG=new A.K("Kids",B.a2m)
B.apF=new A.K("When do notifications come?","By default, a morning briefing at 7:00 and an evening check-in at 21:00. Change the times or turn them off in Settings \u2192 Notifications (Android app).")
B.apK=new A.K("Is there a home screen widget?","Yes, in the Android app. Put the WearCast widget on your home screen to see today's outfit in one line and whether to take an umbrella. It refreshes about every 3 hours.")
B.ap4=new A.K("The weather doesn't update, or refreshing takes long.","The forecast is fetched about every 3 hours; tap refresh at the top right to fetch now. If it can't get one within 15 seconds, it keeps showing the saved forecast \u2014 the time next to the date tells you when that was.")
B.Y5=s([B.apF,B.apK,B.ap4],t.Wy)
B.apP=new A.K("Notifications, widget, refresh",B.Y5)
B.apg=new A.K("How is the web version different from the Android app?","Outfits and the graph are the same. Notifications and the home widget are Android only. On the web, your history stays in that browser and doesn't move to other phones or browsers.")
B.apA=new A.K("Where does my data go?","Only the coordinates for your forecast go to Open-Meteo. Place names, address search and the map also use your rough location. There is no login; your answers and settings stay on your phone.")
B.V1=s([B.apg,B.apA],t.Wy)
B.aog=new A.K("Web and privacy",B.V1)
B.aew=s([B.ap1,B.apJ,B.aoZ,B.aoG,B.apP,B.aog],t.ij)
